# WARP.md

Warp-specific instructions for `{{REPO_NAME}}`. Warp Agent reads this file
when both `AGENTS.md` and `WARP.md` exist in the same directory; per Warp's
documented behavior, `WARP.md` takes priority for Warp Agent (`AGENTS.md`
still applies as the cross-agent baseline).

## Rule Hierarchy

Three rule files coexist in this repo. Read in this order:

1. **`AGENTS.md`** — tool-neutral, all-agent rules. Project identity, conventions,
   constraints. Read first by every agent.
2. **`WARP.md`** (this file) — Warp-specific operator commands and daily workflow.
3. **`CLAUDE.md`** — Claude Code's orchestrator contract. Required for Claude
   Code; ignored by other agents.

## Daily Commands

- `sg` — boot SGSD cockpit + greet Claude in the current terminal.
- `sg -Go` — boot cockpit and send `go` to Claude for autonomous mode.
- `sgsd` — cockpit only.
- `/sgsd-orchestrate go` — start the autonomous SGSD loop.
- `/sgsd-discuss-phase <N>` — gather context before planning a phase.

## Project Shape

This is a SGSD-onboarded repo. The framework lives at `super-gsd/`
(directory junction to the canonical install at `C:\Users\user\GSDedits\super-gsd`).

- `.planning/STATE.md` — current milestone/phase state.
- `.planning/milestones/` — per-milestone plans and phase artifacts.
- `.planning/metrics/` — cockpit, token, Codex, routing, and gate ledgers.
- `super-gsd/` — junction to SGSD framework runtime.

